release: 2026.10.29
resolution: "Delivered by PR #190 (ac6e36e): Forecast Beads producer compatibility before import"
expected_result: Forecast compatibility with named Beads producer dialects before import
actual_result: "PR #190 merged at 2026-10-29T06:26:50Z as ac6e36e; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:52:40.738Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against installed host SDK declarations, package commands and sibling pm-csv, pm-memory, pm-context and pm-ops sources. Host SDK has no named Beads producer forecast; pm-csv dialect descriptors concern table syntax and column mappings. Existing Beads sidecars preserve opted-in unknown top-level JSON; reconciliation, transfers and outgoing deltas exchange canonical snapshots. This feature forecasts named producer compatibility, reusing these mapping and sidecar functions. Forecast is read-only, has no journal or mutable coordinator, and promises no lock isolation; existing transaction leases do not exclude ordinary SDK writers."
  "2026-10-29T01:01:28.025Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only schema-derived producer contracts, deterministic field forecasts, typed remedies and an optional dialect import guard. Exact means canonical mapped state on present fields, not raw JSON spelling. All 17 claimed native names/aliases passed SDK-read import/export/upsert round trips in six real non-git trackers, including CRLF descriptions, blockers, parents and ambient focus. Source status/type, source timestamps, closure audit and ambiguous competing aliases are conservatively unsupported; unknown top-level fields use the existing sidecar. No new leases, checkpoints or mutation journals exist. Existing writer-race tracking remains in pm-beads-51fi and pm-beads-qwvf; this representation guard does not certify transaction isolation."
  "2026-10-29T01:06:04.808Z",codex-agent,"Public validation on frozen main f45fc815: 113 SDK-read records, 72353 native JSONL bytes; full 13-field export contract forecasts exact=9, sidecar-dependent=0, unsupported=4. An explicitly declared 9-field canonical projection passes the shared guard; matching sidecars retain 113 synthetic nested extensions. Full forecast JSON is 2598 bytes; measured analysis 1042.13 ms. Tracker copy is read-only and outside git, git absent from PATH; complete SDK reads and recursive fingerprint prove unchanged state. Focused forecast source coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions (6 passing tests). Behavioral reverts in a disposable non-git copy independently changed exact mapping and removed the unsupported guard: both failed the fixture regression; restoring the fixed implementation passed. The package worktree was never reverted."
  "2026-10-29T01:07:35.239Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed all five real host installation paths (npm global, Bun global, project-local, npx, bunx) with host 2026.10.28, two wire formats each, one unchanged 64-file npm artifact, SHA-256 4d91804ada24463d636e57325f528c46bc81964f998a5004cbcd19ef5236df05. Each report matched the public SDK result and each non-git tracker stayed empty. Expanded focused suite passes 8/8, including 512 generated contract cases and compiled JSON/TOON with git absent. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass; full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T01:17:01.058Z",codex-agent,"PR 190 is ready for review. The targeted 512-sequence SDK-read state-machine test passed (1 test, zero failures/skips), covering native mutation, export, outgoing deltas, reconciliation, upsert, earlier replays, whitespace/CRLF and all touched native relationships/fields; forecast guards run at every state. Focused integration/metadata/flag tests passed 118/118. Final review tightened the blocker domain: opaque native edge nesting and uninterpreted edge kinds refuse through the existing edge mapper. Focused suite now passes 9/9 at 100% forecast-source line/branch/function coverage. Removing the edge guard in a disposable copy fails its new regression; restoring it passes. Final packed acceptance is being refreshed for that change. CI npm/Bun gates remain required at the final pushed head; neutral/skipped reviewers and the expired Greptile trial are not approvals."
  "2026-10-29T01:18:01.283Z",codex-agent,"Final artifact refresh passed all five installation paths and both formats; 64 files, SHA-256 5990506199db096820806df322561619d068164efbaac915b28f2b6ba5373533. Refreshed read-only public validation still reads 113 records / 72353 native bytes, forecasts 9 exact / 4 unsupported fields, validates the explicit 9-field projection and 113 nested sidecars; forecast JSON remains 2598 bytes, measured 1399.16 ms, frozen tracker unchanged. All local work and tracker writes are complete for the final CI head. Full npm/Bun release checks at unchanged thresholds are required on PR 190; their exact-head run URL/counts will be reported in the PR. No merge or release is authorized. Existing ordinary-writer concurrency window is documented; no new SDK gap was found."
  "2026-10-29T01:46:49.550Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR 190 after review. Merged current main first and installed its updated pinned SDK. Class audit: (1) custody receipts must prove current selected values, not only envelope validity or matching ids; ordinary restoration must still allow extensions to be absent after native export. (2) parent references require closure and cycle validation before any new import/plan writes, shared by SDK guards and CLI validation/import. (3) explicit empty collections are replacement operations, distinct from omitted fields, through all aliases and import entry points. Searching sidecar consumers, validators, native/legacy import, transfer/reconciliation/outgoing paths and packed renderers; existing PM item reused, no history rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T02:22:20.706Z",codex-agent,"Review classes: custody now compares current selected-field presence and canonical values, not envelope identity alone; parent closure/cycles are shared pre-write checks in dialect/native validation, effective upserts and reconciliation; explicit empty collections and optional planning strings now replace stored values while omissions retain state. Audited native/legacy commands, SDK, renderers, transfer and outgoing/reconcile paths. No additional actionable nonblocking review findings were present. Added 512 custody transitions, 512 independent parent graphs, receiver-ancestry and empty-value SDK regressions; packed consumer verification is being extended across all five install paths."
  "2026-10-29T02:30:16.344Z",codex-agent,"Focused related validation: npm run build; npm run build:test; npm run docstring (21 source files, 158 documented declarations); node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/forecast-regressions.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts test/repair.test.ts passed 57/57 with zero skips before the final additional ancestry regression. Public read-only non-git validation on main 7f3762d: 113 SDK-read records, 73013 JSONL bytes, 13 fields (9 exact, 4 unsupported), 9-field exact projection accepted, 113 synthetic nested extensions retained, 2598-byte forecast, 14008.70 ms; frozen fingerprint and second complete SDK read unchanged. Local pm health reports installed pm-github host-version skew and an existing provenance advisory; no history repair or toolchain-pin override was made. Fresh CI checkout health remains the release evidence."
  "2026-10-29T02:35:37.783Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: seven independent mutations in a disposable non-git source copy each failed with an assertion (exit 1): remove current selected-value custody; remove source-parent topology; remove effective-upsert parent preflight; remove reconciliation parent preflight; restore truthy-length label import; omit exported empty labels; disable explicit empty planning unsets. Commands used node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern with the matching custody, parent, upsert, reconciliation or empty-alias regression. Restoring fixed source passed node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/forecast-regressions.test.ts (7/7, zero failures/skips). The reviewed worktree was never reverted. The final regression command was also verified by pm test --add with a 600-second timeout; pm test --run --only-index 1 --progress reran the original forecast suite (9/9, zero failures/skips). No tests were deleted or weakened; the warning-path fixture now supplies a real parent so it still tests actual injected SDK write failures rather than structurally invalid input."
  "2026-10-29T02:52:10.585Z",codex-agent,"The must-allow audit caught an introduced preview regression: complete parent graphs with --validate-only tried to list a tracker before initialization. A new real-host test failed before the fix. Optional parent validation now uses the SDK initialization preflight and tolerates only its typed NOT_FOUND result; other read failures stay loud and normal import retains its existing fallback. Both import entry points and SDK validation are checked with absent and empty tracker roots. The first 72-file artifact passed all five launchers and all three review classes; artifact acceptance is being refreshed after this additional compatibility fix."
  "2026-10-29T02:57:52.905Z",codex-agent,"Additional must-allow revert proof: removing only the optional SDK NOT_FOUND handling from readWorkspaceItems in a disposable copy makes the complete-parent-preview regression fail with an assertion (exit 1). Restoring it passes the full review suite, 8/8 with zero failures/skips, including both native/legacy previews before initialization and SDK validation of an empty root. Exact focused command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\\\"complete parent previews\\\" test/forecast-regressions.test.ts. PM-linked verification and run also pass. Ancestry-focused verification additionally passed repeated identities, legacy skip ownership and anonymous upserts. The full suite remains delegated to the unchanged npm/Bun CI release gate with two workers."
  "2026-10-29T03:17:36.737Z",codex-agent,"All three blocking review classes are fixed across audited SDK/native/legacy/validation/reconciliation/output/packed paths; no additional actionable nonblocking finding was present. Final packed acceptance passed all five launchers with host 2026.10.28, both forecast formats and all three review classes. One unchanged 72-file artifact: SHA-256 5b08c2d59f9280eefc7651f0f78c655a0333275a768843611037499a31ff10ff. Eight independent behavioral reverts fail; final restored review suite passes 8/8, zero skips. Related suite passed 57/57; forecast suite 9/9; ancestry and uninitialized-preview checks pass; build, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Copyable preview command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='complete parent previews' test/forecast-regressions.test.ts. Detailed commands, corpora, numbers and proofs are in docs/dialect-forecast-validation.md. Final changelog and workspace/artifact equality checks precede commit. Full npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds and two workers will be verified at the final pushed head; run URL and counts will be recorded in PR 190. Existing ordinary-writer window remains documented and tracked separately; no isolation claim or new SDK gap. Releasing the claim and leaving the item open."
  "2026-10-29T03:22:58.967Z",codex-agent,"The final artifact/workspace comparison caught a documentation sentence edited after capture. A disposable package copy proved that restoring only the validated introductory sentence reproduces the exact tested 72-file artifact SHA-256 5b08c2d59f9280eefc7651f0f78c655a0333275a768843611037499a31ff10ff. Restored that tested wording; the added detailed custody, parent preflight and explicit-empty documentation remains intact. No runtime source or test was weakened. Final byte equality and changelog checks now precede the push; existing history remains append-only."
  "2026-10-29T03:36:24.377Z",codex-agent,"The final class audit found a transient-cycle case beyond static closure: receiver A points to B; source final graph B points to A and A points to C is acyclic, but applying B first can fail while A still points to B. Adding both importer aliases and all six input permutations as an adversarial SDK-read regression. Shared upsert will clear explicitly supplied parent links in the scalar pass before linking the validated final graph, using SDK unset semantics. Omitted parents remain unchanged. This extends the same parent-loss class; current CI is superseded and will be refreshed after focused, packed and revert checks."
  "2026-10-29T03:43:59.084Z",codex-agent,"Superseded CI run 40812152053 completed: both Node versions passed 562/562 tests, zero failures/skips, but unchanged coverage gates correctly refused 99.93% branches / 99.83% functions (lines 100%). Added a real legacy-target parent preview to exercise its ownership skip callback. Removed the obsolete raw-parent passthrough: parent identities are now resolved exclusively from the validated source/SDK receiver map; unknown references refuse before writes. The acyclic rewire regression failed before the shared fix (only 1 of 2 links reported) and now passes both importer aliases over all six input orders. No threshold or test was weakened. Fresh complete gates remain required after the new push."
  "2026-10-29T03:56:39.646Z",codex-agent,"Ninth behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, retaining explicitly supplied nonempty parents in pass one makes the acyclic-parent-rewire regression fail (one of two required links set). Restoring final source passes all 9 review regressions, zero failures/skips. Both importer aliases pass all six input permutations, with parent state read back through the SDK. The focused parent/legacy-preview pair passed 2/2, build and test typecheck pass, docstring lint still reports 21 files / 158 declarations. The new packed artifact already passes npm global, Bun global and project-local, including the valid-rewire case; remaining launchers and final byte equality precede the next push. No shipped file will change after this artifact capture."
  "2026-10-29T04:09:31.142Z",codex-agent,"Final parent-class evidence: all six acyclic-rewire input permutations pass both importer aliases; a ninth independent behavioral revert fails, restored review suite 9/9 with zero skips. PM-linked rewire verification and run pass. Final packed artifact passes all five launchers, both forecast formats, stale-custody/parent/empty-value classes and valid rewires, with SDK read-back. Its 72 shipped files match the captured workspace byte-for-byte; SHA-256 d127a2f189db295795837e3b488989391f9d1cfdf6399e74067ddff517fbb54b. No shipped file changed after capture. The superseded 562-test CI result is not full-gate approval: its unchanged coverage thresholds failed and fresh complete npm/Bun gates will follow this push. Legacy-preview coverage is exercised and unmapped raw-parent fallback is removed; thresholds are unchanged. Existing ordinary-writer window and interrupted multi-step upserts remain documented. Releasing this claim and leaving the item open; exact-head CI URL/counts will be reported in PR 190."
  "2026-10-29T04:43:27.286Z",codex-agent,"CI wait reached the required 30-minute cutoff for source head 495285884f62c6ec648800caab9e276566ffc689. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40816454185: Node 22 npm and Bun release gates each passed 563/563 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across 21 source files, unchanged thresholds. Node 26 remains unverified; last observed queued at 28.4 minutes. Per the queue rule, stop waiting and hand pending verification to the orchestrator pipeline. This receipt-only commit changes no runtime, tests or shipped artifact; it will trigger fresh exact-head CI, which is also pending. PR 190 records source-head evidence separately from the receipt head. No gate is inferred from missing results. Releasing the claim and leaving the item open; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T05:03:56.956Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 resumed: the reviewed worktree is clean and current with origin/main. General rules: deferred relationship writes must use the final effective edit per target, including clears and omissions; relationship identities must cross native/external namespaces exactly once. Auditing shared import, reconciliation, previews, SDK and CLI outputs, and packed consumers; adding adversarial SDK readback and behavioral revert proofs for both classes."
  "2026-10-29T05:10:59.309Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 audit: both native and legacy importers share one apply path. Deferred parent edits now select the last explicitly supplied parent per native target; omitted/null parents preserve the prior explicit edit, and empty parents cancel it. Blocker replacements select the final successful target edit and report only effective edges. Shared parent validation composes duplicate patches instead of unioning superseded edges. Reconciliation validates canonical external parents without a second native translation. Import preview/apply alias tables now seed native fallback first and canonical external aliases second, using the same first-owner index as upsert. Export and transfer already translate relationships once; forecast snapshots require unique identities. Published review threads contain no additional actionable non-blocking findings. New tests cover 512 duplicate graphs, 64 seeded real-SDK duplicate trajectories, both schemas and reconciliation aliases, and native/external collisions in both receiver orders. Existing tests remain intact; the 512-sequence state model now also replays earlier duplicate parents before final clear/replacement rows."
  "2026-10-29T05:19:57.621Z",codex-agent,"Focused validation passed: duplicate-target and reconciliation namespace tests 2/2, zero failures/skips; separate effective-graph and importer-namespace tests 2/2, zero failures/skips. The former includes 64 seeded SDK-reference trajectories; the latter includes 512 generated duplicate graphs. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check pass. Local strict health has intact history/integrity but fails the existing pm-github extension/host version skew; a foreign provenance warning is retained. Fresh CI health will be reported separately. Linked regression timeouts were extended for the expanded real-SDK corpus on the saturated shared host, without altering tests or coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T05:25:23.286Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof (disposable non-git copy only): five independent reversions each failed its adversarial regression with exit 1. Replaying every deferred parent restored an earlier link after a later clear; replaying every blocker replacement reported duplicate effective edges; unioning superseded source edges refused a valid effective graph; translating canonical reconciliation parents a second time refused the native/external collision; restoring interleaved native/external alias insertion refused a valid import. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=<pattern> test/forecast-regressions.test.ts; patterns duplicate target rows, 512 duplicate parent, reconciliation keeps external, and import parent namespaces. The fixed implementation is restored in the disposable copy and its full 13-test review suite is running. The reviewed worktree was never reverted. Linked pm test --run --only-index 3 --progress passed 1/1, zero failures/skips; test-result persistence remains disabled to keep scratch paths out of tracker content."
  "2026-10-29T05:47:01.532Z",codex-agent,"Restoration verified: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/forecast-regressions.test.ts passed 13/13, zero failures/cancellations/skips, in the restored disposable copy. All five Round 2 independent behavioral reverts fail as recorded; the reviewed implementation was never reverted. Both global packed consumers and project-local acceptance pass so far on the single unchanged artifact; npx and bunx are still running. New state cases and original nine review regressions all remain enabled at unchanged coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T06:01:18.336Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 complete locally: all 13 restored review regressions pass with zero failures/cancellations/skips; all five behavioral reverts fail. The unchanged 72-file npm artifact passed npm global, Bun global, project-local, npx and bunx with host 2026.10.28, JSON/TOON, real non-git SDK readback, duplicate clears, changed and retained identity collisions, both importer aliases and both saved-plan reconciliation aliases. SHA-256 85589a54513353d644376d14c472f76b302e8caef07142473665ff713db42d87; every shipped file equals the final workspace. Existing 512-sequence state-model coverage now includes earlier duplicate parent and label inputs before final replacements. No existing test or threshold was weakened. Files/docs/tests are linked, append-only history and public-path checks pass. Fresh npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 must certify the final pushed head; exact run receipts will be reported on PR 190 and in the final response. Local extension/host skew is retained separately; ordinary SDK writers still have a documented read/write window. No merge or release."
